# semaphore-flags

Feature-flag + kill-switch service. TypeScript (strict, ESM, Node 22) · Fastify 5 · Zod ·
Postgres 16 · optional Redis 7 · Vitest · OpenAPI · pnpm.

Read before non-trivial work: `openspec/config.yaml`, `docs/architecture/README.md`, and the
relevant `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.

## Workflow

- OpenSpec gate: new endpoints, migrations, evaluate semantics, error codes, cache keys, metrics
  or contract fixtures require an approved change in `openspec/changes/<change-id>/` first.
  Use Fission OpenSpec: `/opsx-propose`, `/opsx-apply`, `openspec validate`, `/opsx-archive`
  (see `openspec/README.md`).
- Cite SRS ids (`FR-EVAL-002`) in proposals, tests and PR descriptions.
- Before declaring done: `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build`.
- Keep `docs/architecture/` and `.cursor/rules/` in sync when a convention changes.

## Git

- Conventional commits with intent: `feat(evaluate): bucket users by sha256 of salt:key:id`.
  Types: feat, fix, refactor, test, docs, chore, ci, build, perf.
- Branches: `chore/…`, `feat/…`, `test/…`, `docs/…`. One theme per PR; small PRs.
- Author/committer is the repo owner's configured identity. Never add AI/agent authors or
  `Co-authored-by` trailers.
- Never commit secrets or `.env`. Never rewrite published history.

## Scope guards (do not build)

Admin SPA, multivariate/string variants, experimentation stats, streaming or native SDKs, rule
builder UI, multi-region, ORM, DI container. HTTP is the SDK.

## Non-negotiables

- `src/domain` is pure: no I/O, no Fastify, no `pg`/Redis, no imports from outer layers.
- Evaluate on a missing flag returns `200 { value: false, reason: "not_found" }`.
- Evaluate never fails because Redis is down.
- Admin mutation + its audit row share one transaction; cache invalidated before 2xx.
- Audit rows are never updated or deleted.
- Parameterized SQL only.
